  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"1.0.3\"\n\n# v1 (rattler-build) recipe. conda-forge/staged-recipes requires this format for\n# new submissions -- the old conda-build v0 meta.yaml format is deprecated for\n# new recipes. Usable today for local testing with rattler-build\n# (`pixi global install rattler-build && rattler-build build --recipe\n# conda-recipe/recipe.yaml -c conda-forge`); intended as the direct basis for\n# a future conda-forge/staged-recipes submission, which is a separate,\n# manual maintainer step (needs its own PR review process there) and not\n# something this recipe does on its own. See RELEASING.md for the full\n# release process.\n\npackage:\n  name: pamtra\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/igmk/pamtra/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 81a30557fe7e1ecdb0db7b9d01b30d8e201bbae6f64ac8e3c5e2bceb81ea4c65\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  # meson.build's openblas fallback logic prefers an env-local libopenblas\n  # (this recipe's own host dependency) over pkg-config or Homebrew, so no\n  # extra environment wiring is needed here for that.\n  skip:\n    # PAMTRA has never been built on Windows (no Windows CI in the\n    # upstream repo) and its Fortran code hasn't been verified against\n    # MSVC. Revisit once someone can actually test a Windows build.\n    - win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('fortran') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - pkg-config\n    - ninja\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - meson-python\n    - cython\n    - numpy\n    - netcdf4\n    - libopenblas\n    - fftw\n    # meson.build unconditionally adds -lz for zlib, which needs the\n    # unversioned libz.so symlink from `zlib` (not just the runtime\n    # libzlib.so.1) to be present at link time.\n    - zlib\n    # libnetcdf is intentionally not listed explicitly -- it's pulled in\n    # transitively via netcdf-fortran. Listing it here would make\n    # conda-forge's global pinning force an exact libnetcdf version, which\n    # can be newer than what the current netcdf4 (Python bindings) build\n    # supports, making the environment unsolvable.\n    - netcdf-fortran\n  run:\n    - python\n    # numpy is intentionally not listed here either -- it has run_exports\n    # set (see conda-forge/numpy-feedstock), so host: numpy already pulls\n    # a properly-versioned constraint into run: automatically.\n    - scipy\n    - netcdf4\n    - matplotlib-base\n    # libopenblas and netcdf-fortran are intentionally not listed here --\n    # both have run_exports set, so listing them in host: already pulls\n    # them into run: automatically with an appropriate version constraint.\n    - pooch\n    - tqdm\n\ntests:\n  # PAMTRA_DATADIR must be set (even to \"\") before `import pyPamtra` --\n  # otherwise it tries to auto-fetch external data over the network, which\n  # isn't appropriate for a package test -- see conftest.py's\n  # PAMTRA_DATADIR handling for why the test suite always sets this first.\n  - script:\n      - PAMTRA_DATADIR=\"\" python -c \"import pyPamtra\"\n      # --rootdir=. pins pytest's config discovery to the test working\n      # directory -- without it, pytest walks upward past a local `path: ..`\n      # build dir (nested inside this checkout) and picks up this repo's\n      # own pyproject.toml as rootdir instead.\n      - PAMTRA_DATADIR=\"\" pytest tests -v --rootdir=.\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - pytest\n    files:\n      source:\n        - tests\n        - descriptorfiles\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/igmk/pamtra\n  license: GPL-3.0-only\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Passive and Active Microwave TRAnsfer radiative transfer model\n  description: |\n    Python/Fortran 90 package to solve the passive and active microwave\n    radiative transfer in a plane-parallel horizontally homogeneous\n    atmosphere with hydrometeors.\n  documentation: https://pamtra.readthedocs.io/\n  repository: https://github.com/igmk/pamtra\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - maahn\n",
